stream
BT
/F1 20.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 742.00 Tm (Chapter 4 Consensus) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 728.00 Tm (Consensus lets replicas agree on one value even when some nodes fail or messages are delayed.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 714.00 Tm (Safety means no two replicas commit different values; liveness means progress while a majority is alive.) Tj
/F1 14.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694.40 Tm (4.1 Paxos) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 680.40 Tm (Paxos runs Prepare and Accept phases before a value is chosen.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 666.40 Tm (A proposer first collects promises from a majority, then broadcasts the value it intends to commit.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 652.40 Tm (It guarantees safety only; liveness relies on randomized retries and an extra leader election layer.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 638.40 Tm (Paxos is famous for being hard to understand and hard to extend into a replicated log.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
