stream
BT
/F1 14.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 750.40 Tm (4.3 ZAB) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 736.40 Tm (ZAB is the atomic broadcast protocol used by ZooKeeper.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 722.40 Tm (It separates recovery mode from broadcast mode and orders committed transactions.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 708.40 Tm (A new leader must synchronise its log with the previous leader before serving writes.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694.40 Tm (ZAB guarantees that committed transactions are delivered in the same order to every replica.) Tj
/F1 10.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 680.40 Tm (ZooKeeper builds locks, leader election and configuration management on top of this ordered log.) Tj
ET
endstream
